        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "ci: add GitHub Pages deploy workflow for website",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n- Publishes the `website/` app through GitHub Pages at the canonical public URL, `https://voxcli.sh`.\n- Uses one Pages workflow with current action majors, read-only Pages metadata access in the build job, deployment-only Pages/OIDC write permissions, and manual recovery dispatch.\n- Builds from the Pages-configured base path, so custom-domain `/` and repository fallback `/vox/` assets both resolve correctly.\n- Fixes the preloader, favicon, canonical URL, and social-image paths; verifies the generated HTML, JavaScript assets, and CNAME artifact.\n- Removes the unused Netlify and Vercel deployment configurations so GitHub Pages is the single hosting contract.\n\n## User impact\n\nThe merged Vox marketing site gains an owned deployment path and canonical URL instead of remaining only a buildable repository subproject. Changes under `website/` publish automatically after the deployment build, typecheck, and artifact checks pass.\n\n## Hosting contract\n\n- Canonical URL: `https://voxcli.sh`\n- Publisher: GitHub Pages, using GitHub Actions\n- Domain artifact: `website/public/CNAME`\n- Base path: supplied by `actions/configure-pages`, not hardcoded\n- Build permissions: `contents: read` and `pages: read`\n- Deploy permissions: `pages: write` and `id-token: write`\n\n## Proof\n\nExact head: `3c992b98629aab36dc4ffe247ff3bc552e8f743b`\n\n- Root: frozen install, format/lint, typecheck, 61/61 tests, and production build pass.\n- Website: frozen install and typecheck pass.\n- Production builds for `/` and `/vox/` pass.\n- Deploy verifier confirms favicon/assets, preloader logo, CNAME, canonical URL, and social metadata for both bases.\n- `actionlint` passes for CI and deploy workflows.\n- Structured Codex autoreview: clean for the focused permission fix and the full branch; no accepted/actionable findings.\n- Source-blind artifact checks return HTTP 200 for the `/vox/` page, logo, social image, CSS, JavaScript, and CNAME; an intentionally missing asset returns 404.\n- Existing-Chrome proof renders the full landing page after refresh, with a 150×150 loaded logo and the expected canonical URL.\n- Exact-head [GitHub CI](https://github.com/steipete/vox/actions/runs/28513677170) passes on Node 22, Node 24, website build/deploy verification, and GitGuardian.\n- Repository Pages settings use GitHub Actions with `voxcli.sh` as the custom domain.\n- Live deployment proof is blocked only by public DNS: the apex still resolves to Namecheap URL forwarding, `www` aliases Namecheap parking, and HTTPS is unavailable.\n\n## Required repository setup\n\nReplace the current Namecheap URL-forwarding DNS with GitHub Pages apex A/AAAA records and `www` CNAME `steipete.github.io`. After propagation and certificate issuance, enable HTTPS and run live browser proof before merge unless that proof is explicitly waived.\n",
